db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464010} {:answer/id #uuid "394ae117-d4ca-5aaa-996a-0e62be1d057f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "394ae117-d4ca-5aaa-996a-0e62be1d057f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464011} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6432d3b-3369-5a1b-8709-7139b2ad5f94" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b463b24-e0d7-56c4-b957-08fba1ac548b" :question/math-academy-id "q-134105" :question/problem "![](images/57/5768d8f90d3dd754471a69d25582eca6cdb2f4993b9b22020dc9f2038aa61954.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above summarizes data collected by a Midwestern high school showing the relationship between the number of absences in a month and the class size. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one class reported a total of $6$ absences in the month.\n- Two classes have a total of $20$ students each.\n- Only one class has more than $24$ students.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is false. The scatter plot has two points whose vertical coordinate is equal to $6,$ namely, $(16,6)$ and $(20,6).$ This means that two of the classes each reported a total of 6 absences in the month.\n\n![](images/a6/a62b1d5a63764b38013fdbdba9ba85a4495cd996a2d9f975dbe3d7eb89166234.png)\n\n  \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $20,$ namely, $(20,6).$ This means that only one of the classes has a total of  $20$ students.\n\n![](images/3c/3c41f2e111ef141511ec4f2faa655ddcea8f2b7e0b73bd37f0b1e142d5d60f14.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. From the scatter plot, only one class has more than $24$ students. This class is represented by the point to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](images/ad/adcba37370fdac69b152a8d18ef710d5f665d9a3252376ea312808be7d08a407.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268967 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec401b55-8663-5101-8b41-59b151a26397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464012} {:answer/id #uuid "9bdaed2c-2c6d-5426-a191-bf8506a45bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bdaed2c-2c6d-5426-a191-bf8506a45bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464013} :answer-field/id #uuid "14320a73-82dc-573d-a1b5-29d902fab9cc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464940} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "279d29a8-30d4-542a-baed-fa528ceb8976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464014} {:answer/id #uuid "436ebb22-e532-5f6b-92fb-8ea8c4228586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "279d29a8-30d4-542a-baed-fa528ceb8976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464014} :answer-field/id #uuid "22a6c85f-945a-5314-b9c3-d095bdda11bc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464941} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82efdbc7-b79d-5892-bab3-c0f3a146c24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464016} {:answer/id #uuid "c63b57f5-d326-5335-a378-99b6e341e5b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82efdbc7-b79d-5892-bab3-c0f3a146c24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464016} :answer-field/id #uuid "02e25783-e60a-569d-91d3-f16eb94bbc63" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464942}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a188568f-e246-50ee-bc75-14d95b670306" :question/math-academy-id "q-134128" :question/problem "![](images/69/69517e814dae28db96c64a662ce97b5fc40ea10355cb5a02561a0d12e1a3f845.png)\n\nA math teacher asked his students how many hours of sleep they had the\nnight before a test. The information he received is summarized in the scatter plot above.\n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- Only one student obtained a score of $90.$\n- Only one student slept for $6$ hours.\n- None of the students obtained a score lower than $75.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $90,$ namely, $(7,90).$ This means that only one student obtained a score of $90.$\n\n![](images/ef/ef915015fa9c7685f45f26ee9cd2c10dfce5a4253aed22b6ea2ea57f0c3c26e2.png)\n\n    \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has two dots whose horizontal coordinate equals $6,$ namely, $(6,80)$ and $(6,85).$ This means that two students had  $6$ hours of sleep.\n\n![](images/31/3139ca71a780b76ca7355ddd119d6502f1cd390d67064db3a4a57801e33f2917.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, three students obtained a score lower than  $75.$  Those students are represented by the three dots below the horizontal line.\n\n![](images/a6/a675a94a9183a86d221bb2199dae38f9f55b9f91dff9868320b0b8f4d38b3fe9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152234 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35453324-c2ff-5be4-86aa-70b3085154dc" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Information From a Scatter Plot"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72fd5fd6-0272-562c-955a-ecfbd0be0499" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464018} {:answer/id #uuid "bdcbfbe5-836a-5a0a-bc7d-81d56e1af9e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdcbfbe5-836a-5a0a-bc7d-81d56e1af9e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464019} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c2546bb-7c09-5638-8414-f31ba655b999" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464943} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "372ab02c-1479-55a5-95fe-a30edcf5594f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464020} {:answer/id #uuid "85f9397b-5dae-5414-96bb-7fe9eb1790e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "372ab02c-1479-55a5-95fe-a30edcf5594f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464020} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdf2a422-ef07-5243-a01a-2134809e5de6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464944} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b045124-c41a-572a-90bd-f6d3a3ad2f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464022} {:answer/id #uuid "612f0081-90e4-5e24-a884-beee4ea2164e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b045124-c41a-572a-90bd-f6d3a3ad2f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464022} :answer-field/id #uuid "559a390b-361c-5e77-86df-9051726c5e55" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26f51f13-3f23-54c9-b7ba-52010958ad0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-134139" :question/problem "![](images/37/376bd65db6b1d0a91c6013462e686ffad4d8acceee4948e61cf291d6403a12cd.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above is based on data collected from several homes in a given community. It shows the relationship between the age of a house and the number of people living in it. \n\nGiven that none of the points overlap, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- There is only one house where precisely $3$ people live.\n- Two of the houses are $16$ years old.\n- Only one house is older than $24$ years old.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our scatter plot.\n\n- Statement I is true. The scatter plot has only one dot whose vertical coordinate equals $3,$ namely, $(18,3).$ This means that there is only one house where $3$ people live.\n\n![](images/7a/7a56236f0c5649a64436809b2a5e1fb8f00ed3d345cd81c571f96d579d6c19b6.png)\n\n \n\n- Statement II is false. The scatter plot has only one dot whose horizontal coordinate equals $16,$ namely, $(16,6).$ This means that only one house is $16$ years old.\n\n![](images/6d/6d9a60cd10c6d7cc9f9d51d0be44c32cb688e19da988b3e84b30f0c4be32a2a8.png)\n\n- Statement III is false. From the scatter plot, two houses are more than $24$ years old, represented by the two dots to the right of the vertical line.\n\n![](images/44/44b7395bb2e5ee0a71899869e6caedb949e8744adde314134f6a09e4c8f8a35d.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269024 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124615 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f2f4f4-af4a-597d-b6c6-afb82e708fc2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Steady-State Vectors of Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fab7f30-6daa-5568-b92a-c8222dbff730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464024} {:answer/id #uuid "693c3e17-97fa-51ee-90dc-89044808a0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "693c3e17-97fa-51ee-90dc-89044808a0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464025} :answer-field/id #uuid "81a3115e-2494-5d9d-933b-598d187f85cb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464946} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae0f49bf-0cd6-54f7-8f07-c3e4c2a0820e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464026} {:answer/id #uuid "edde4065-f83b-537f-b778-128d3d7e37bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edde4065-f83b-537f-b778-128d3d7e37bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464027} :answer-field/id #uuid "c06fe170-3e20-5457-900e-718afcde8f0d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464947} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "319d511e-1cf0-56b4-8aff-8cd32c8fecef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464028} {:answer/id #uuid "17e9985b-24ce-5cf5-ab6d-998a5381b5c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17e9985b-24ce-5cf5-ab6d-998a5381b5c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464029} :answer-field/id #uuid "80e294d2-17d3-5a25-b256-c28be00fc333" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464948}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c393953b-f9cd-55bd-bdae-3a3a7283cff2" :question/math-academy-id "q-135306" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.85\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} \\\\ \\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- **II.** $Pq=q$\n- **III.** $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have \n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.2 & 0.85\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} \\\\ \\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2.4}{7}+\\frac{0.6}{7} \\\\ \\frac{0.6}{7}+\\frac{3.4}{7}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} \\\\ \\frac{4}{7}\\end{aligned}]=q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector such that $Pq=q.$ So, it's a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124615 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f2f4f4-af4a-597d-b6c6-afb82e708fc2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Steady-State Vectors of Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50cf12ba-0f8c-5d6a-86d7-d5466a1a1711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464030} {:answer/id #uuid "766369ab-0fe7-5050-9921-76a53d28350f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "766369ab-0fe7-5050-9921-76a53d28350f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464031} :an