5307" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.7\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 0.8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- **II.** $Pq=q$\n- **III.** $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 & 0.3 \\\\ 0.9 & 0.7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.2 \\\\ 0.8\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.02+0.24 \\\\ 0.18+0.56\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.26 \\\\ 0.74\\end{aligned}]\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124615 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4f2f4f4-af4a-597d-b6c6-afb82e708fc2" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Steady-State Vectors of Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8516fd9-972d-5124-9e1f-77abae39069f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464036} {:answer/id #uuid "073c821c-d49c-5876-a77b-1da4d5924a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "073c821c-d49c-5876-a77b-1da4d5924a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464037} :answer