field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "05952a75-ee49-5c6e-985c-55f5554bd3f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-135311" :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.15 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.7 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.15 & 0.05\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- **II.** $Pq=q$\n- **III.** $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Note that\n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.3 & 0.15 & 0.6 \\\\ 0.6 & 0.7 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.1 & 0.15 & 0.05\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0.1 \\\\ 0.7 \\\\ 0.2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.03+0.105+0.12 \\\\ 0.06+0.49+0.07 \\\\ 0.01+0.105+0.01\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0.255 \\\\ 0.62 \\\\ 0.125\\end{aligned}]\\ne q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $Pq\\ne q,$ it is not a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66b24a98-c641-5e08-8bec-30f221d1bb22" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Stochastic Vectors and Stochastic Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8786cf44-21c3-5f91-ae1e-9ed86d4c4ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "fals