-88f5-ab03da770a79" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f670c211-dff8-5382-9b62-e560f1a2abfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-158425" :question/problem "![](images/87/87c5e1b3307b2a42fff6a97408c0475dbe242bef4a9dbfbabcec407b3fa23ce1.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{3},\\, & 0\\le x<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, we see that $f(x)$ is nonnegative for all $x.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}(1)^{4}-\\frac{3}{4}(0)^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278180 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16a6f0f7-4003-5908-8b1b-68d218fdcb8f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdd36874-a5b3-5b80-9397-bf4e44707f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464582} {:answer/id #uuid "84b4cb88-d37a-5d13-9e42-faa7c4544bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84b4cb88-d37a-5d13-9e42-faa7c4544bb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464583} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b856ade-7fe2-5349-a5a5-28bb1ff57ab0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465225} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e40683af-6d4d-52b9-b123-d349c1ed7f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464584} {:answer/id #uuid "278bd59e-8031-5311-b4f7-7e46f395b899" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e40683af-6d4d-52b9-b123-d349c1ed7f70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464584} :answer-field/id #uuid "7694657f-6b3e-5e1d-8795-49e2cb21539d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465226} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84082a42-31b8-551d-9a57-581a0ec2cd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464586} {:answer/id #uuid "04586925-a18f-5497-a4b9-7966350140ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84082a42-31b8-551d-9a57-581a0ec2cd10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464586} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5005a3e-0368-554b-b05a-c2142332dc1c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ba85730-5b8d-5d4c-8799-b386e641d64f" :question/math-academy-id "q-158427" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae6d25fae4127a74b38bcb9c0de8f44705dca81353c89557047e5d35a3465c5b.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x,\\, & 1\\le x\\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, we see that $f(x)$ is nonnegative for all $x.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16a6f0f7-4003-5908-8b1b-68d218fdcb8f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d069b6d-1b28-5ce7-bf94-b37a8e291cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464588} {:answer/id #uuid "199e07b4-fdc2-520a-860d-5661e00a77c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d069b6d-1b28-5ce7-bf94-b37a8e291cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464588} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4c96219-e0b3-5dc7-8dc7-69c5722fa7b6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccaefb5b-cfb4-52d2-be52-7e73358d6eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464590} {:answer/id #uuid "057798e9-f16d-5452-9025-2419284bee6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464591}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "057798e9-f16d-5452-9025-2419284bee6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464591} :answer-field/id #uuid "d855d726-8725-5fca-a081-8879d5d230a6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc175dc9-39c4-5b61-ae58-cabe869e8c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464592} {:answer/id #uuid "6a338737-2e5b-5530-96cb-fb44a251a025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc175dc9-39c4-5b61-ae58-cabe869e8c8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464592} :answer-field/id #uuid "736d1c64-48e3-5924-98c2-79e6482564e4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50d76297-0f50-5089-b83a-de45e6a36bc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-158428" :question/problem "![](images/6e/6e540dc9309f2a5d1753760b4050c049e380705914d7289b47319de0b0696a9a.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4({x}^{3}-1),\\, & \\frac{1}{2}<x\\le \\frac{3}{2}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{1/2}^{3/2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. $f(x)$ is negative for some value of $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/2}^{3/2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{3/2}4({x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{1/2}^{3/2}({x}^{3}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-x]}_{1/2}^{3/2} \\\\  & =4([\\frac{81}{64}-\\frac{3}{2}]-[\\frac{1}{64}-\\frac{1}{2}]) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{80}{64}-1) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{5}{4}-1) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement I is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278182 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16a6f0f7-4003-5908-8b1b-68d218fdcb8f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcaf39e0-215e-5bcb-9f69-b79d4fea6fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464594} {:answer/id #uuid "fc883669-b6bd-50ff-84a1-40c6f677f746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc883669-b6bd-50ff-84a1-40c6f677f746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464595} :answer-field/id #uuid "11957c19-83b4-50d8-b41f-1092eb031c39" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "787e3253-5ff2-5136-99a3-45a1fcefd8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464596} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6eee04-9be6-5e85-a684-d1532f141746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "787e3253-5ff2-5136-99a3-45a1fcefd8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464596} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea00921e-a75c-5d04-a5db-9162d91c392a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eea68c3-ecab-5537-8997-6369ca24cce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464598} {:answer/id #uuid "519e2afc-3cba-585d-b51a-f0ae9f20f329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1eea68c3-ecab-5537-8997-6369ca24cce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464598} :answer-field/id #uuid "e686a893-1ac9-5401-87b5-12b786a36222" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0715ac14-20ca-5be9-8d09-d1a1ccc33941" :question/math-academy-id "q-158429" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0c30c392223857c77cfc8619f1fa0d4b7fca20af618bdd424570cc3ed712f38b.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2x-1,\\, & 1<x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, we see that $f(x)$ is nonnegative for all $x.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{2}-x]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[9-3]-[1-1] \\\\  & =6-0 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34c9c06-e884-5758-a184-39330a07d8cd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points of Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c6e0563-60fe-573a-be2b-c09286e0d28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464600} {:answer/id #uuid "8e161fc7-1d15-5bde-b789-e5538def14f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e161fc7-1d15-5bde-b789-e5538def14f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464601} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed0c0536-5566-58ba-9627-1a27b29de0e8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82cac744-5325-5785-87eb-888aa14491a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464602} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf113b9-f90e-5668-ae93-83231d949649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaf113b9-f90e-5668-ae93-83231d949649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464603} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fd29ecd-65da-5acc-9237-ce8e9eac3252" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce6d1aa5-a903-545d-8b95-75b53ca2b13b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464604} {:answer/id #uuid "d7f38a1c-72a0-5e6b-9320-c6e45960b272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7f38a1c-72a0-5e6b-9320-c6e45960b272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464605} :answer-field/id #uuid "001728ff-5f50-5db0-b0d4-7cdfa3b9596d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed33ac2f-6299-5342-b520-1399b2a77786" :question/math-academy-id "q-158684" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5dccdb1f8957bb15d7b2215320c6e632819a647bf4dc350ff850876bae6298ec.png)\n\nConsider the set $M=(-3,2]$ and the points $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is a boundary point of the set $M$\n- $B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$\n- $C$ is an interior point of the set $M$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}\\in R$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is *smaller than* $\\delta :$ \n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nA neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is given by the open interval $({x}_{0}-\\delta ,{x}_{0}+\\delta ),$ shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f889352f25e7936d0e5ea76585a979efbb301da61f7e99a937e979af93ee0664.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The point $A$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $A$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\n![](images/d5/d595e29d31743694c404b99c79c60e40b152d30083e633d4269ad4444be3f826.png)\n\n- Statement II is true. The point $B$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $B$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\n![](images/23/2336ff8a65dd397e8324384b9f9536f3c7d4ad2d76a81caeba28d7fe3ec229ef.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. The point $C$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $C$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\n![](images/26/26903667d45cecf81539025c4cda333129cf89600821b383f20d574c75e537b0.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I, II, and III.'"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124635 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34c9c06-e884-5758-a184-39330a07d8cd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Interior and Boundary Points of Sets of Real Numbers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96356f47-c178-5a33-bb0a-25787d54b790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464606} {:answer/id #uuid "d261f82c-07fe-537e-a6d4-ea593eb568c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d261f82c-07fe-537e-a6d4-ea593eb568c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464607} :answer-field/id #uuid "be11caff-d2e8-5f49-9988-c418cfadb534" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae5e3317-6cb6-5f5d-8f8d-a588ac041b89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464608} {:answer/id #uuid "3edad2c7-dffb-510f-b03c-c40ad14a1dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae5e3317-6cb6-5f5d-8f8d-a588ac041b89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464608} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a3d15ba-67d5-501c-b3be-022701568e8c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c485ad6-9c4f-5370-b143-0ce473c05f30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464610} {:answer/id #uuid "e530432f-f73f-5284-bec5-159f1f6c1026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e530432f-f73f-5284-bec5-159f1f6c1026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464611} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1229fa5-9182-533b-9908-fc72ca3ea300" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1861489-bfb5-5c9b-ba84-97990e733cb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-158685" :question/problem "![](images/73/73f61de1a716545449439ed8875b465dc5aec6f3148e520ad028a96725f2a4f0.png)\n\nConsider the set $M=[0,1]\\cup {2}$ and the points $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is an interior point of the set $M$\n- $B$ is an interior point of the set $M$\n- $C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}\\in R$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is *smaller than* $\\delta :$ \n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nA neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is given by the open interval $({x}_{0}-\\delta ,{x}_{0}+\\delta ),$ shown below.\n\n![](images/f8/f889352f25e7936d0e5ea76585a979efbb301da61f7e99a937e979af93ee0664.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The point $A$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $A$ that is fully contained in the set $M.$\n\n![](images/84/84afb5331ef9244120d9f3d9b14e25fa2d19da31f8eb685c5d74b089e0d99289.png)\n\n- Statement II is false. The point $B$ is *not* an interior point of $M$ since any neighborhood of $B$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\n![](images/c0/c0b35fafc6e628c36e41fa8df42e3a477d8aac4af0b4c3819fa0063e5bd014df.png)\n\n- Statement III is true. The point $C$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $C$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$ Notice that $C$ is a point of $M$ and $C$ belongs to any open neighborhood of $C.$\n\n![](images/e5/e54fa85543a79c18e00d3b03281d6774c98fdb03e9b5440b8f179ce5a0d09519.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'I and III only.'"}]}
